{% comment %}
  Renders one customer review: the quote, then the reviewer's avatar, name and
  role at the foot of the card.

  The card is pure presentation — it holds no review content of its own and knows
  nothing about the marquee it usually sits in, so it is equally at home in a
  grid, a slider or on its own. Everything it looks like comes from
  --review-card-* custom properties with defaults, which means a section can
  restyle every card by emitting tokens on an ancestor without this snippet
  changing. Requires assets/component-review-card.css.

  Accepts:
  - quote:       {String} The review text. Escaped, with line breaks preserved.
    Ignored when quote_html is given. (optional)
  - quote_html:  {String} Pre-formatted review markup, e.g. from a `richtext`
    setting or a product-review metafield. Rendered as-is. (optional)
  - name:        {String} Reviewer's name. (optional)
  - role:        {String} Reviewer's role, company or location. (optional)
  - avatar:      {Object} Image. Preferred over avatar_url — it is served
    responsively. (optional)
  - avatar_url:  {String} Image url, for review data that arrives as plain
    strings rather than as Shopify images. (optional)
  - avatar_alt:  {String} Overrides the avatar's alt text. Defaults to the
    image's own alt, then to the reviewer's name. (optional)
  - quote_marks: {Boolean} true wraps the quote in typographic quotation marks.
    Default false. (optional)
  - clamp:       {Boolean} true caps the quote at --review-card-quote-clamp
    lines. Default false. (optional)
  - lazy_load:   {Boolean} false loads the avatar eagerly. Default true.
    (optional)

  Usage:
    render 'review-card', quote: block.settings.quote, name: block.settings.name,
      role: block.settings.role, avatar: block.settings.avatar
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign reviewer_name = name | strip
  assign reviewer_role = role | strip

  assign avatar_alt_text = avatar_alt | default: avatar.alt
  assign avatar_alt_text = avatar_alt_text | default: reviewer_name | default: ''

  comment
    An avatar is a portrait of the person named right beside it, so an empty alt
    would be defensible — but a name in the alt is what makes the picture
    meaningful when the card is read out of context, e.g. in a search result.
  endcomment

  assign avatar_loading = 'lazy'
  if lazy_load == false
    assign avatar_loading = 'eager'
  endif

  assign card_classes = 'review-card'
  if quote_marks
    assign card_classes = card_classes | append: ' review-card--quoted'
  endif
  if clamp
    assign card_classes = card_classes | append: ' review-card--clamped'
  endif
-%}

<figure class="{{ card_classes }}">
  {%- if quote_html != blank or quote != blank -%}
    <blockquote class="review-card__quote">
      {%- if quote_html != blank -%}
        {{ quote_html }}
      {%- else -%}
        <p>{{ quote | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </blockquote>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if reviewer_name != blank or reviewer_role != blank or avatar != blank or avatar_url != blank -%}
    <figcaption class="review-card__author">
      {%- if avatar != blank -%}
        {{
          avatar
          | image_url: width: 160
          | image_tag:
            loading: avatar_loading,
            class: 'review-card__avatar',
            widths: '40, 60, 80, 120, 160',
            sizes: '80px',
            alt: avatar_alt_text
        }}
      {%- elsif avatar_url != blank -%}
        <img
          class="review-card__avatar"
          src="{{ avatar_url }}"
          alt="{{ avatar_alt_text | escape }}"
          loading="{{ avatar_loading }}"
          width="80"
          height="80"
        >
      {%- elsif reviewer_name != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Initial in place of a missing photo: it holds the avatar's box, so the
          names and roles stay on the same baseline right across a row whether or
          not every reviewer supplied a picture. Decorative — the name it stands
          for is read out immediately after it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="review-card__avatar-fallback" aria-hidden="true">
          {{- reviewer_name | slice: 0 | upcase -}}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if reviewer_name != blank or reviewer_role != blank -%}
        <span class="review-card__identity">
          {%- if reviewer_name != blank -%}
            <span class="review-card__name">{{ reviewer_name | escape }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if reviewer_role != blank -%}
            <span class="review-card__role">{{ reviewer_role | escape }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </figcaption>
  {%- endif -%}
</figure>
